summary:
  The heal commit gate goes back to trusting a shared streaming host as
  the station's own domain, so a name-matched tenant of zeno.fm can
  overwrite the user's saved station permanently.

history:
  Found in the 2026-08-20 search-and-heal review. The old gate compared
  base domains and nothing else; on multi-tenant hosts the comparison is
  a landlord check, not an identity check — measured from the catalog's
  3000 most-voted stations, streamtheworld.com alone houses 171 distinct
  stations and zeno.fm 163. A "Smooth Jazz Radio" living at the same
  landlord as the user's dead "Jazz" scored contains+sameBase and walked
  through the permanent-write door; the notification then claimed the
  user's station had moved. This mutant removes the landlord refusal.

target:
  package/contents/ui/HealLogic.js

find:
      if (sharedBase(oldBase)) return "stopgap";

replace:
      if (false) return "stopgap";

expect:
  Killed by tst_heallogic.qml
  test_the_commit_gate_demands_identity_not_similarity: the zeno.fm
  exact-name case must answer "stopgap". Line-neutral.
